  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Monday)\n\nUpper level trough is beginning its trek through the southwestern\nUS this morning as light showers are ongoing across western \nNevada. The GFS and ECMWF have continued to track the trough \nmoving SW down the California coast before bringing it inland \nacross far southern Nevada and into Arizona by Tuesday morning. \nHowever, just as it exits Nevada, this trough will tap into \ntropical moisture from Hurricanes Odalys and Polo, which will lead\nto a excessive rainfall for Utah, Arizona, and points east. That \nbeing said, there is a 20% to 60% chance for light isolated to \nscattered showers with a few thunderstorms accompanying trough \npassage late Sunday night through early Tuesday morning. However \nthe best chances at seeing rain has trended south across central \nNevada, with thunderstorm chances limited to the southern portions\nof NE Nye, and White Pine counties.. Amounts still look light \nwith a trace to 0.05\u201d for northern Nevada, while central Nevada \nmay see a trace up to 0.35\u201d for the mountains of Great Basin \nNational Park. Tuesday through next weekend models return ridging \nover much of the southwestern US, but there is still a bit of \ndisagreement on orientation of the upper flow as solutions vary \nfrom NW to SW flow aloft. Temperature wise, a cooling trend lasts \nthrough Tuesday, with highs falling into the mid 70s. Wednesday \nwill start a new slow warming trend, with the return of upper \nridging as highs return to the lower 80s. Lows will range in the \nmid to upper 40s for the first half of the forecast period, \ncooling into the mid to upper 30s by middle of next week.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n \nThere is high confidence in the potential for a 20% chance for \nisolated showers across northern Nevada, and a 30% to 60% chance \nfor isolated to scattered showers and thunderstorms across central\nNevada Monday.\n\nThere is high confidence in the return of upper level ridging for\nthe middle of next week restoring quiet and dry pattern over \nNevada.",
